[size=5][b]Enshwick for Vortex[/b][/size]

This extension lets Vortex install [url=https://enshwick.com]Enshwick[/url] and Enshwick mods for Enshrouded. Enshwick is a mod loader and modding framework.

[size=4][b]What does it install?[/b][/size]
[list]
[*]It puts powrprof.dll beside the game and the loader in mods/enshwick/.
[*]It puts each Enshwick mod into its own folder, mods/<mod id>/.
[*]It keeps files such as LICENSE out of the game folder.
[*]It asks you to confirm before it installs powrprof.dll, because that file runs with the game.
[*]It warns you when Enshwick mods are on and Enshwick is not.
[/list]
The extension downloads nothing. It installs the files you download.

[size=4][b]What you need[/b][/size]
[list]
[*]Vortex 2.10.1 or newer.
[*]The Enshrouded game extension, [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/site/mods/2453]mod 2453 in Modding Tools[/url]. It adds Enshrouded to Vortex. This extension works beside it.
[/list]

[size=4][b]How do I install it?[/b][/size]
[list=1]
[*]In Vortex, open Extensions.
[*]Drag this file's zip onto Drop File(s).
[*]Restart Vortex.
[*]Manage Enshrouded under Games.
[*]Download Enshwick as the [url=https://enshwick.com/guides/install/]install guide[/url] shows.
[*]Install Enshwick, then each mod, with Install From File on the Mods page.
[*]Select Install when Vortex asks about powrprof.dll.
[*]Turn the mods on and select Deploy Mods.
[/list]

[size=4][b]How do I remove it?[/b][/size]
Turn Enshwick or a mod off in Vortex, then select Deploy Mods. Purge Mods removes every file Vortex deployed.

[size=4][b]Source[/b][/size]
The source is on [url=https://github.com/enshwick/vortex-extension]GitHub[/url], under the MIT licence.
